{"title":"IAT (IISER)","category":"Engineering","bank":"iat_iiser","subject":"Biology","chapter":"Biomolecules (B)","count":7,"questions":[{"id":23809,"subject":"Biology","chapter":"Biomolecules (B)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"IAT (IISER)","q":"The diagram represents an enzyme, its substrate and potential inhibitors (P, Q, R, S, T).<br/><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fiat%252FqbU8AtD6Iyk0YkrcqLpcfzcckv9pb3ZYDeHRHZFM7is.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fiat%2FqbU8AtD6Iyk0YkrcqLpcfzcckv9pb3ZYDeHRHZFM7is.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fiat%2FqbU8AtD6Iyk0YkrcqLpcfzcckv9pb3ZYDeHRHZFM7is.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>Which one of the following combinations is the best pair of competitive inhibitors for the enzyme?","options":["$\\mathrm{R}, \\mathrm{T}$","$\\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{R}$","$\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{S}$","$\\mathrm{S}, \\mathrm{T}$"],"answer":2,"solution":"No solution available. ","difficulty":"Medium","source":"IAT (IISER) 2023","_marksId":"67fdff6c378e1624ea7b6b4d"},{"id":23810,"subject":"Biology","chapter":"Biomolecules (B)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"IAT (IISER)","q":"Which of the following products are expected when lipase acts on diglycerides?","options":["Fatty acids and glucose","Glucose and galactose","Monoglycerides and glycerol","Fatty acids and glycerol"],"answer":3,"solution":"No solution available. ","difficulty":"Easy","source":"IAT (IISER) 2020","_marksId":"67fdff58378e1624ea7b6a79"},{"id":23811,"subject":"Biology","chapter":"Biomolecules (B)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"IAT (IISER)","q":"Match the entries in column I and column II. Which one of the following choices is correct?<br/><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fiat%252FIJM-hUJT10AYdQd0PMTBFHSIpVjGo2kwDWv9dA9z7X4.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fiat%2FIJM-hUJT10AYdQd0PMTBFHSIpVjGo2kwDWv9dA9z7X4.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fiat%2FIJM-hUJT10AYdQd0PMTBFHSIpVjGo2kwDWv9dA9z7X4.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>","options":["$\\mathrm{a}-3, \\mathrm{ b}-1, \\mathrm{c}-4, \\mathrm{ d}-2$","$\\mathrm{a}-4, \\mathrm{ b}-3, \\mathrm{c}-1, \\mathrm{ d}-2$","$\\mathrm{a}-2, \\mathrm{ b}-1, \\mathrm{c}-3, \\mathrm{ d}-4$","$\\mathrm{a}-4, \\mathrm{ b}-1, \\mathrm{c}-3, \\mathrm{ d}-2$"],"answer":1,"solution":"No solution available. ","difficulty":"Medium","source":"IAT (IISER) 2019","_marksId":"67fdff51378e1624ea7b6a17"},{"id":23812,"subject":"Biology","chapter":"Biomolecules (B)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"IAT (IISER)","q":"For which one of the following enzyme activity plots, will the $K_m$ of the enzyme for substrate 'S' be 20? [S] indicates substrate concentration.","options":["<img style=\"width: 300px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-c6d19a28d6e53da1.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-c6d19a28d6e53da1.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-c6d19a28d6e53da1.png\">","<img style=\"width: 300px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-dfde6ddc0fcbd3b6.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-dfde6ddc0fcbd3b6.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-dfde6ddc0fcbd3b6.png\">","<img style=\"width: 300px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-396203045632c821.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-396203045632c821.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-396203045632c821.png\">","<img style=\"width: 300px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-493d42acbf542071.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-493d42acbf542071.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-493d42acbf542071.png\">"],"answer":0,"solution":"The Michaelis constant ($K_m$) is defined as the substrate concentration $[S]$ at which the reaction velocity ($V$) is half of its maximum velocity ($V_\\max$).<br><br>From the given plots, the maximum velocity is indicated by the dashed line:<br>$V_\\max = 16$<br><br>Therefore, half of the maximum velocity is:<br>$\\dfrac{V_\\max}{2} = \\dfrac{16}{2} = 8$<br><br>We need to find the plot where the velocity is $8$ when the substrate concentration $[S]$ is $20$.<br><br>Looking at the given options:<br>In plot (a), the curve passes exactly through the point $(20, 8)$. This means at $[S] = 20$, $V = 8$, which corresponds to $\\dfrac{V_\\max}{2}$. Thus, $K_m = 20$.<br>In plot (b), at $[S] = 40$, $V = 8$, so $K_m = 40$.<br>In plot (c), at $[S] = 5$, $V = 8$, so $K_m = 5$.<br>In plot (d), at $[S] \\approx 35$, $V = 8$, so $K_m \\approx 35$.<br><br>Hence, the first plot correctly represents an enzyme with $K_m = 20$.<br><br>Answer: <img style=\"width: 300px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-c6d19a28d6e53da1.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-c6d19a28d6e53da1.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-c6d19a28d6e53da1.png\">","difficulty":"Medium","source":"IAT (IISER) 2026","_marksId":"6a4521828c20d3b91d64f953","answers":[0],"questionType":"singleCorrect"},{"id":23813,"subject":"Biology","chapter":"Biomolecules (B)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"IAT (IISER)","q":"Match the biomolecules given in Column I with their corresponding chemical nature given in Column II.<br/><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fiat%252F824S2J4JSBN5n5pBHLDF1_5e3Sjn6-T1yPLpbwZKDpc.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fiat%2F824S2J4JSBN5n5pBHLDF1_5e3Sjn6-T1yPLpbwZKDpc.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fiat%2F824S2J4JSBN5n5pBHLDF1_5e3Sjn6-T1yPLpbwZKDpc.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>Which one of the following combinations is correct?","options":["$P - (i); Q - (iii); \\mathbb{R} - (ii); S - (iv)$","$P - (iv); Q - (ii); \\mathbb{R} - (i); S - (iii)$","$P - (ii); Q - (iv); \\mathbb{R} - (iii); S - (i)$","$P - (iii); Q - (i); \\mathbb{R} - (iv); S - (ii)$"],"answer":1,"solution":"No solution available. ","difficulty":"Medium","source":"IAT (IISER) 2023","_marksId":"67fdff6b378e1624ea7b6b44"},{"id":23814,"subject":"Biology","chapter":"Biomolecules (B)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"IAT (IISER)","q":"If an enzyme reaction follows the Michaelis Menten kinetics represented by the equation: $V_0=V_{\\max } \\cdot \\frac{[S]}{K_M+[S]}$<br/>where, $V_0$ is the initial reaction velocity,<br/>$V_{\\max }$ is the maximal reaction velocity,<br/>$K_M$ is the Michaelis constant and $[S]$ is the substrate concentration.<br/>Which of the following statements is correct?","options":["$K_M$ is the concentration of the enzyme at the optimal pH.","$K_M$ is the reaction velocity at half the optimal substrate concentration.","$K_M$ is the concentration of substrate when the velocity of the reaction is half that of the maximal velocity.","$K_M$ is the concentration of the enzyme at the optimal temperature."],"answer":2,"solution":"No solution available. ","difficulty":"Easy","source":"IAT (IISER) 2017","_marksId":"67fdff3c378e1624ea7b691d"},{"id":23815,"subject":"Biology","chapter":"Biomolecules (B)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"IAT (IISER)","q":"Which compound given below inhibits cholesterol synthesis in humans?","options":["Streptokinase","Statins","Penicillin","Cyclosporin A"],"answer":1,"solution":"No solution available. ","difficulty":"Easy","source":"IAT (IISER) 2018","_marksId":"67fdff4a378e1624ea7b69b5"}]}